## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:functionality_1_user_login  
Pseudocode:  
```
FUNCTION login(username, password)  
    IF AuthManager.validate_login(username, password)  
        SET session['username'] = username  
        REDIRECT to home  
    ELSE  
        RENDER login.html WITH error="Invalid credentials"  
    ENDIF  
ENDFUNCTION  

CLASS AuthManager  
    FUNCTION validate_login(username, password)  
        IF users.txt EXISTS  
            FOR EACH user IN users.txt  
                IF user['username'] == username AND user['password'] == password  
                    RETURN True  
                ENDIF  
            ENDFOR  
        ENDIF  
        RETURN False  
    ENDFUNCTION  
ENDCLASS  
```
Key Libraries:  
- `flask.session` (manages user sessions)  
- `json` (parses user credentials from file)  

Alternative Implementation:  
```
CLASS TaskManager:
    FUNCTION login(username, password):
        users = READ users.txt (FORMAT: username|password|email)
        IF username IN users AND users[username]['password'] == password:
            RETURN True
        ELSE:
            RETURN False

ROUTE /login (POST):
    username = FORM['username']
    password = FORM['password']
    IF TaskManager.login(username, password):
        SET session['username'] = username
        REDIRECT /home
    ELSE:
        RENDER login.html WITH error="Invalid credentials"
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask (`session`) – Manages user sessions after successful login.  

---

2. |Case|:functionality_2_user_registration  
Pseudocode:  
```
FUNCTION register(username, password, email)  
    IF AuthManager.register_user(username, password, email)  
        REDIRECT to login  
    ELSE  
        RENDER register.html WITH error="Registration failed"  
    ENDIF  
ENDFUNCTION  

CLASS AuthManager  
    FUNCTION register_user(username, password, email)  
        IF username OR password OR email MISSING  
            RETURN False  
        ENDIF  

        IF users.txt EXISTS  
            FOR EACH user IN users.txt  
                IF user['username'] == username  
                    RETURN False  
                ENDIF  
            ENDFOR  
        ENDIF  

        APPEND new_user = {'username': username, 'password': password, 'email': email} TO users.txt  
        RETURN True  
    ENDFUNCTION  
ENDCLASS  
```
Key Libraries:  
- `json.dumps()` (stores user data in JSON format)  

Alternative Implementation:  
```
CLASS TaskManager:
    FUNCTION register(username, password, email):
        users = READ users.txt (FORMAT: username|password|email)
        IF username IN users:
            RETURN False
        ELSE:
            APPEND username|password|email TO users.txt
            RETURN True

ROUTE /register (POST):
    username = FORM['username']
    password = FORM['password']
    email = FORM['email']
    IF TaskManager.register(username, password, email):
        REDIRECT /login
    ELSE:
        RENDER register.html WITH error="Username already exists"
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask (`redirect`, `url_for`) – Handles page redirection after registration.  

