## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:functionality_3_view_task_list  
Pseudocode:  
```
FUNCTION home()  
    IF session['username'] NOT SET  
        REDIRECT to login  
    ENDIF  

    tasks = TaskManager.get_tasks(session['username'])  
    RENDER home.html WITH username=session['username'], tasks=tasks  
ENDFUNCTION  

CLASS TaskManager  
    FUNCTION get_tasks(username)  
        IF tasks.txt EXISTS  
            FOR EACH task IN tasks.txt  
                IF task['username'] == username  
                    ADD task TO tasks_list  
                ENDIF  
            ENDFOR  
        ENDIF  
        RETURN tasks_list  
    ENDFUNCTION  
ENDCLASS  
```
Key Libraries:  
- `flask.render_template` (renders HTML with dynamic data)  

Alternative Implementation:  
```
CLASS FileStorage:
    FUNCTION read_tasks():
        tasks = []
        READ tasks.txt (FORMAT: username|description|due_date|task_id)
        FOR EACH LINE:
            SPLIT INTO username, description, due_date, task_id
            APPEND TO tasks LIST
        RETURN tasks

CLASS TaskManager:
    FUNCTION get_tasks(username):
        ALL_TASKS = FileStorage.read_tasks()
        RETURN FILTER tasks WHERE task['username'] == username

ROUTE /home (GET):
    IF 'username' NOT IN session:
        REDIRECT /login
    ELSE:
        tasks = TaskManager.get_tasks(session['username'])
        RENDER home.html WITH username, tasks
```
Key Libraries:  
- Flask (`session`) – Ensures only logged-in users can view tasks.  

