## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:functionality_5_remove_task  
Pseudocode:  
```
FUNCTION remove_task(task_index)  
    IF session['username'] NOT SET  
        REDIRECT to login  
    ENDIF  

    TaskManager.remove_task(session['username'], task_index)  
    REDIRECT to home  
ENDFUNCTION  

CLASS TaskManager  
    FUNCTION remove_task(username, task_index)  
        IF tasks.txt EXISTS  
            FOR EACH task IN tasks.txt  
                IF task['username'] == username  
                    IF task_index == 0  
                        REMOVE task  
                        SET removed = True  
                    ELSE  
                        DECREMENT task_index  
                    ENDIF  
                ENDIF  
            ENDFOR  
        ENDIF  

        IF removed  
            REWRITE tasks.txt WITHOUT removed task  
            RETURN True  
        ENDIF  
        RETURN False  
    ENDFUNCTION  
ENDCLASS  
```
Key Libraries:  
- File I/O operations (rewriting `tasks.txt`)  

Alternative Implementation:  
```
CLASS FileStorage:
    FUNCTION delete_task(task_id):
        ALL_TASKS = read_tasks()
        UPDATED_TASKS = FILTER OUT task WHERE task['task_id'] == task_id
        REWRITE tasks.txt WITH UPDATED_TASKS
        RETURN True

CLASS TaskManager:
    FUNCTION remove_task(task_id):
        RETURN FileStorage.delete_task(task_id)

ROUTE /home (POST):
    IF 'task_id' IN FORM:
        task_id = FORM['task_id']
        TaskManager.remove_task(task_id)
    REDIRECT /home
```
